A struct stored whole carries its fields with it: they are instances of the
same field locations, so a copy (*dst = *src) or a struct returned by a
function the analysis sees (make1) adds no value that the field's writers did
not store. A struct that comes from a call with no Candidates is built by
code the analysis does not see: the field keeps an Unresolved entry next to
the values found.
